{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgLR26dpgoVb3jfCmTqje","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is PR #2731 (merge commit `1f4098170806704451ed195a9922dc1a30ebcedc`, ticket O3-5958). It changed the new queue entry form's default queue location so it starts from the location the Service Queues dashboard resolved and stored, instead of only the login location.\n\n**The fix**\n\n- The form's `defaultValues` now reads `queueLocation: selectedQueueLocationUuid ?? sessionLocation?.uuid ?? ''` (`openmrs-esm-patient-management/packages/esm-service-queues-app/src/create-queue-entry/queue-fields/queue-fields.component.tsx:81`). Before the fix it was `sessionLocation?.uuid ?? ''`.\n- The same file now pulls `selectedQueueLocationUuid` from `useServiceQueuesStore()` (line 68).\n- The PR changed two files: that component, and `queue-fields.test.tsx`, which gained 17 lines of tests for the pre-fill behaviour.\n\n**Why the dashboard value was available**\n\n- The dashboard header resolves the login location if it is queue-tagged, otherwise its nearest queue-tagged ancestor, otherwise \"All\" (`openmrs-esm-patient-management/packages/esm-service-queues-app/src/patient-queue-header/queue-location-header-title.component.tsx:35-41`).\n- It stores that result via `updateSelectedQueueLocationUuid` (same file, line 56; the store function is in `packages/esm-service-queues-app/src/store/store.ts:45`).\n\n**Review history**\n\n- The first version of the PR used a `useEffect` that re-applied the session location. Reviewer dkayiwa pointed out that this overrode user selections and made the \"Select a queue location\" option unpickable. The author dropped the effect in favour of the `defaultValues` change, and the PR title and description were corrected to match.\n\nI did not check out the merged code to run the tests.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-management/packages/esm-service-queues-app/src/create-queue-entry/queue-fields/queue-fields.component.tsx\", \"startLine\": 81, \"endLine\": 81},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-management/packages/esm-service-queues-app/src/create-queue-entry/queue-fields/queue-fields.component.tsx\", \"startLine\": 68, \"endLine\": 68},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-management/packages/esm-service-queues-app/src/patient-queue-header/queue-location-header-title.component.tsx\", \"startLine\": 35, \"endLine\": 41},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-management/packages/esm-service-queues-app/src/patient-queue-header/queue-location-header-title.component.tsx\", \"startLine\": 56, \"endLine\": 56},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-management/packages/esm-service-queues-app/src/store/store.ts\", \"startLine\": 45, \"endLine\": 45},\n  {\"repo\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-management\", \"pr\": 2731},\n  {\"repo\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-management\", \"commit\": \"1f4098170806704451ed195a9922dc1a30ebcedc\"},\n  {\"ticket\": \"O3-5958\"}\n]\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1175,"cache_read_input_tokens":26129,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1175},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4dd46c0c-2f26-451c-bd3a-0e7e711e5a66","uuid":"25bd10fa-6d5b-40d0-8d6a-6d9cd814b07e","timestamp":"2026-10-24T04:16:14.288Z","request_id":"req_011CgLR26QRsJYwtzeNC6GKX"}
